    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register Patient",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"registers with 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "",
                  "if (res && res.data && res.data.accessToken) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", res.data.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", res.data.refreshToken || \"\");",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "packages": {},
                "requests": {}
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"Patient1\",\n    \"email\": \"mentor.saminravi@gmail.com\",\n    \"password\": \"12345678\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/register",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "5000",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: **201**. In one Prisma transaction this creates a `User` (`role: PATIENT`, `status: ACTIVE`, `emailVerified: false`, `authProvider: CREDENTIALS`, bcrypt-hashed password) and its matching `Patient` row.\n\nReturns `data: { accessToken, refreshToken, user, patient }`, and also sets both tokens as cookies. The test script stores the tokens in collection variables for the protected requests below.\n\nThere is no email verification step — the OTP/verify-email/forget-password/reset-password flows went away with better-auth."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Credential Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();\n\npm.test(\"logs in with 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));\n\nif (res && res.data && res.data.accessToken) {\n    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", res.data.accessToken);\n    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"refreshToken\", res.data.refreshToken || \"\");\n}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"sohagali@gmail.com\",\n    \"password\": \"12345678\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1/auth/login",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": [
                "localhost"
              ],
              "port": "5000",
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Expected: 200 with `data: { accessToken, refreshToken, user }`.\n\nOther outcomes from `AuthService.loginUser`:\n- unknown email → 404 \"User not found\"\n- `status: BLOCKED` → 403 \"User is blocked\"\n- `isDeleted` or `status: DELETED` → 404 \"User is deleted\"\n- account with no password (Google-only sign-in) → 400 \"This account uses Google sign-in. Please continue with Google.\"\n- wrong password → 401 \"Invalid credentials\""
          },
          "response": []
        },
